{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Tollmaster's Bargain","logline":"As the skybridges fray, cartographer Veya and toll-master Kael clash over charts and tolls that keep the bridges standing but starve The Hollow, forcing the isles to decide whether the man who bleeds them is also the one who saves them.","theme":"Control and sharing both carry a cost, and no saviour is spotless.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Price of Passage","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_charting_the_fade","title":"Charting the Fade","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight to read the colours of the currents and finds that several key skybridges are failing faster than the Wardens admit. Her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart looks confirmed.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and confirm her mentor's theory.","conflict":"Her readings contradict the official Warden surveys. She is too stubborn to doubt her own interpretation, and she knows the charts could be dangerous if mishandled.","outcome":"Veya completes a draft chart showing the last stable routes converging on a few crossings, and resolves to take it to Mistral Docks to verify the routes."},{"id":"scn_kaels_ledger","title":"Kael's Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael tallies the season's tolls and wind-debts. He calculates that the repair levy barely covers the failing bridges and that the Cartel's monopoly will not survive a collapse. He decides the last stable routes must be seized.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize the last stable skybridge routes to secure the Cartel's monopoly before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery shows him the weakest points in the system, but he equates price with worth. The only way to fund repairs is to raise tolls on isles that already cannot pay.","outcome":"Kael raises the tolls on grain crossings to the Hollow, setting the grain levy in motion, and sends word to learn who is mapping the bridges."},{"id":"scn_hollow_ration","title":"The Hollow Goes Hungry","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris watches the millers cut rations as the raised tolls make grain shipments unaffordable. She starts using her knowledge of unmapped service corridors to move grain in secret.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers already watch the main routes. Maris trusts slowly, so she has no one to share the risk with.","outcome":"Maris completes a first, narrow smuggling run, but a Cartel enforcer sees her tracks and the levy tightens.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"Old Apprentices","summary":"Veya reaches Mistral Docks to check her routes against shipping records. Kael meets her openly, charming and courteous, and recalls their apprenticeship. He offers to buy her charts, admiring her skill but unable to let her succeed on her own terms.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the shipping records to verify her routes. Kael wants her charts under Cartel control.","conflict":"Veya refuses to let Kael control the charts. Kael needs them but dares not show how much he needs them.","outcome":"Veya leaves without selling. Kael tells his enforcers to watch her, and Veya realises the Cartel wants the charts buried.","depends_on":["scn_charting_the_fade","scn_kaels_ledger"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Bridges and Bargains","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_accusation","title":"Sabotage at the Forge","summary":"At Emberroost, the Bridge Wardens tell Veya that cloudstone cable deliveries have been delayed and blame Kael for sabotaging forge-island supplies. Veya sees the cable stock for herself and finds the shortage is real and that the toll-funded repairs are failing.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Learn whether the Cartel is sabotaging repairs, and test her chart against the cables that hold the bridges.","conflict":"The Wardens want her chart as a weapon against the Cartel. Veya fears becoming an ambitious leader herself and cannot admit that Kael's tolls might be the only thing funding the cable.","outcome":"Veya learns the cable stock holds only a few more seasons, and that without Kael's tolls it would already have run out. She keeps this to herself.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_maris_meets_veya","title":"Secret Paths","summary":"Veya follows the hunger to The Hollow and meets Maris. They trade wind-current knowledge for the service corridors, and Veya sees how thin the grain stocks are.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the unmapped corridors for her chart. Maris wants safe grain routes and a way to avoid the enforcers.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and fears Veya's charts could expose her smuggling. Veya hesitates to share her own findings.","outcome":"They agree to an alliance. Veya's wind-sight and Maris's paths yield a hidden route, but Veya has still not told Maris what she learned at Emberroost.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_ration","scn_emberroost_accusation"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_close_in","title":"The Closing Net","summary":"Kael's enforcers, guided by his reading of the grain trade, intercept a smuggling run between the Hollow's windmills. Maris escapes using her corridors, but a granary is seized under the grain levy and a wind-debt is called in against her family.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to enforce the levy and stop the smuggling that undermines Cartel revenue. Maris wants to save the grain.","conflict":"Kael sees only price and ledgers, while Maris sees her neighbours going hungry. She trusts no one and blames Veya for the leak.","outcome":"The granary is lost. Maris suspects Veya's charts exposed her routes, straining their alliance and pushing the Hollow Circle to open resistance.","depends_on":["scn_maris_meets_veya","scn_docks_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_charts_dispute","title":"The Wrong Reading","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya's rechecked charts show that one of the routes she gave Maris was wrong, because of a misread current. She will not admit the error, and the mistake has cost the Hollow grain.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Prove her mentor's theory and defend her chart against Warden doubts.","conflict":"Her flaw, being unable to admit she is wrong, keeps her from correcting the chart or warning Maris, even as evidence mounts.","outcome":"Veya buries the error in a footnote and tells herself it can wait, setting up a break with Maris and a choice between recognition and honesty.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_kael_offers_bargain","title":"The Tollmaster's Offer","summary":"Kael finds Veya at Mistral Docks as a bridge span cracks nearby. He lays out the numbers: his tolls pay for every cable, and he offers to waive the Hollow's levy if she hands over the full charts and the secret routes.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts to claim the last stable routes. Veya wants a safe route and the Hollow spared.","conflict":"The bargain would feed the Hollow but give the Cartel total control. Kael admires her skill, yet cannot let her chart stand independent. Veya cannot admit her error to bargain honestly.","outcome":"Veya refuses and flees, but Kael has seen the wrong reading and quietly files it, knowing he now holds a weakness.","depends_on":["scn_charts_dispute","scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_maris_confronts_veya","title":"Broken Trust","summary":"Maris finds Veya at Mistral Docks and accuses her of leaking the routes. Veya's refusal to admit the wrong reading nearly ends the alliance, until Maris sees the footnoted correction.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants the truth about the lost granary. Veya wants to keep the alliance without confessing.","conflict":"Maris rarely forgives, while Veya's pride makes her defensive, and Kael's enforcers are close.","outcome":"Veya finally admits the error, an unwelcome first step. Maris, torn between home and friendship, agrees to one more run, and the two plan to cross the failing bridges together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_bargain","scn_charts_dispute"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Breaking Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_bridge_collapse","title":"The Last Stable Crossing","summary":"On the crossing between Emberroost and The Hollow, a span begins to fail. Veya reads the wind to guide a convoy of grain and refugees, Maris leads them along service corridors, and Kael arrives with his enforcers to seize the crossing.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to get the grain across safely. Kael wants to seize the last stable route.","conflict":"Kael's seizure would close the crossing and starve the Hollow, but his tolls are the only thing funding the repair cable. Veya must share her full chart to guide the crossing, which means giving up control of it.","outcome":"Veya hands her full charts to the crowd, including Kael, and her wind-sight guides everyone off the span before it fails.","depends_on":["scn_maris_confronts_veya","scn_kael_offers_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_kaels_choice","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"In the aftermath at Emberroost, Kael stands over the broken span with the ledger in his hand and Veya's charts before him. He sees that seizing the routes would cost more than it gains, and must choose between his monopoly and the isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael must decide whether to enforce the monopoly or share control. Veya wants the charts used for the whole archipelago.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and cannot easily let go, and Veya must trust the man who starved the Hollow.","outcome":"Kael suspends the grain levy and agrees to fund repairs through a shared toll, with the Wardens and the Hollow Circle watching the ledger.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_collapse"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Isles Owe","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Across the Sky","summary":"Grain moves openly to the isles under the reduced levy. Maris helps the Hollow Circle restock the granaries, and realises that hiding, like standing still, can be a brave act, even if it is no longer needed.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the Hollow's food supply under the new arrangement.","conflict":"Hunger has left scars, and Maris, who rarely forgives, must decide whether to trust Veya and Kael's bargain.","outcome":"Maris keeps her corridors secret but opens the granaries, and her friendship with Veya survives with honest terms.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_ledger","title":"Truths Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the full charts, including the error she once hid, and the Academy starts teaching them. She accepts recognition shared with Maris and the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Publish the charts and settle her mentor's legacy.","conflict":"Her pride and fear of becoming like the Cartel leaders pull against publishing an admission of wrong.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and her mentor's theory is accepted with her correction attached.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_docks_reckoning","title":"The Tollmaster's Bargain","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the isles gather to judge Kael. The Cartel is angry at his concession, the Hollow wants the toll abolished, and the Wardens say the bridges need his tolls. Kael accepts both blame and praise, his charm gone quiet.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle whether Kael remains toll-master under the shared arrangement.","conflict":"No one can agree whether he is villain or saviour. The tolls fund the bridges that also drain the Hollow.","outcome":"Kael keeps the post under shared oversight. The isles accept the bittersweet bargain, and Kael learns that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest","scn_silverspine_ledger"]}]}]}
</Output>
