s no one and blames Veya for the leak.","outcome":"The granary is lost. Maris suspects Veya's charts exposed her routes, straining their alliance and pushing the Hollow Circle to open resistance.","depends_on":["scn_maris_meets_veya","scn_docks_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_charts_dispute","title":"The Wrong Reading","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya's rechecked charts show that one of the routes she gave Maris was wrong, because of a misread current. She will not admit the error, and the mistake has cost the Hollow grain.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Prove her mentor's theory and defend her chart against Warden doubts.","conflict":"Her flaw, being unable to admit she is wrong, keeps her from correcting the chart or warning Maris, even as evidence mounts.","outcome":"Veya buries the error in a footnote and tells herself it can wait, setting up a break with Maris and a choice between recognition and honesty.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_kael_offers_bargain","title":"The Tollmaster's Offer","summary":"Kael finds Veya at Mistral Docks as a bridge span cracks nearby. He lays out the numbers: his tolls pay for every cable, and he offers to waive the Hollow's levy if she hands over the full charts and the secret routes.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts to claim the last stable routes. Veya wants a safe route and the Hollow spared.","conflict":"The bargain would feed the Hollow but give the Cartel total control. Kael admires her skill, yet cannot let her chart stand independent. Veya cannot admit her error to bargain honestly.","outcome":"Veya refuses and flees, but Kael has seen the wrong reading and quietly files it, knowing he now holds a weakness.","depends_on":["scn_charts_dispute","scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_maris_confronts_veya","title":"Broken Trust","summary":"Maris finds Veya at Mistral Docks and accuses her of leaking the routes. Veya's refusal to admit the wrong reading nearly ends the alliance, until Maris sees the footnoted correction.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants the truth about the lost granary. Veya wants to keep the alliance without confessing.","conflict":"Maris rarely forgives, while Veya's pride makes her defensive, and Kael's enforcers are close.","outcome":"Veya finally admits the error, an unwelcome first step. Maris, torn between home and friendship, agrees to one more run, and the two plan to cross the failing bridges together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_bargain","scn_charts_dispute"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Breaking Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_bridge_collapse","title":"The Last Stable Crossing","summary":"On the crossing between Emberroost and The Hollow, a span begins to fail. Veya reads the wind to guide a convoy of grain and refugees, Maris leads them along service corridors, and Kael arrives with his enforcers to seize the crossing.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to get the grain across safely. Kael wants to seize the last stable route.","conflict":"Kael's seizure would close the crossing and starve the Hollow, but his tolls are the only thing funding the repair cable. Veya must share her full chart to guide the crossing, which means giving up control of it.","outcome":"Veya hands her full charts to the crowd, including Kael, and her wind-sight guides everyone off the span before it fails.","depends_on":["scn_maris_confronts_veya","scn_kael_offers_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_kaels_choice","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"In the aftermath at Emberroost, Kael stands over the broken span with the ledger in his hand and Veya's charts before him. He sees that seizing the routes would cost more than it gains, and must choose between his monopoly and the isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael must decide whether to enforce the monopoly or share control. Veya wants the charts used for the whole archipelago.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and cannot easily let go, and Veya must trust the man who starved the Hollow.","outcome":"Kael suspends the grain levy and agrees to fund repairs through a shared toll, with the Wardens and the Hollow Circle watching the ledger.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_collapse"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Isles Owe","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Across the Sky","summary":"Grain moves openly to the isles under the reduced levy. Maris helps the Hollow Circle restock the granaries, and realises that hiding, like standing still, can be a brave act, even if it is no longer needed.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the Hollow's food supply under the new arrangement.","conflict":"Hunger has left scars, and Maris, who rarely forgives, must decide whether to trust Veya and Kael's bargain.","outcome":"Maris keeps her corridors secret but opens the granaries, and her friendship with Veya survives with honest terms.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_ledger","title":"Truths Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the full charts, including the error she once hid, and the Academy starts teaching them. She accepts recognition shared with Maris and the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Publish the charts and settle her mentor's legacy.","conflict":"Her pride and fear of becoming like the Cartel leaders pull against publishing an admission of wrong.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and her mentor's theory is accepted with her correction attached.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_docks_reckoning","title":"The Tollmaster's Bargain","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the isles gather to judge Kael. The Cartel is angry at his concession, the Hollow wants the toll abolished, and the Wardens say the bridges need his tolls. Kael accepts both blame and praise, his charm gone quiet.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle whether Kael remains toll-master under the shared arrangement.","conflict":"No one can agree whether he is villain or saviour. The tolls fund the bridges that also drain the Hollow.","outcome":"Kael keeps the post under shared oversight. The isles accept the bittersweet bargain, and Kael learns that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest","scn_silverspine_ledger"]}]}]}
