g the routes. Veya's refusal to admit the wrong reading nearly ends the alliance, until Maris sees the footnoted correction.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants the truth about the lost granary. Veya wants to keep the alliance without confessing.","conflict":"Maris rarely forgives, while Veya's pride makes her defensive, and Kael's enforcers are close.","outcome":"Veya finally admits the error, an unwelcome first step. Maris, torn between home and friendship, agrees to one more run, and the two plan to cross the failing bridges together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_bargain","scn_charts_dispute"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Breaking Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_bridge_collapse","title":"The Last Stable Crossing","summary":"On the crossing between Emberroost and The Hollow, a span begins to fail. Veya reads the wind to guide a convoy of grain and refugees, Maris leads them along service corridors, and Kael arrives with his enforcers to seize the crossing.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to get the grain across safely. Kael wants to seize the last stable route.","conflict":"Kael's seizure would close the crossing and starve the Hollow, but his tolls are the only thing funding the repair cable. Veya must share her full chart to guide the crossing, which means giving up control of it.","outcome":"Veya hands her full charts to the crowd, including Kael, and her wind-sight guides everyone off the span before it fails.","depends_on":["scn_maris_confronts_veya","scn_kael_offers_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_kaels_choice","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"In the aftermath at Emberroost, Kael stands over the broken span with the ledger in his hand and Veya's charts before him. He sees that seizing the routes would cost more than it gains, and must choose between his monopoly and the isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael must decide whether to enforce the monopoly or share control. Veya wants the charts used for the whole archipelago.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and cannot easily let go, and Veya must trust the man who starved the Hollow.","outcome":"Kael suspends the grain levy and agrees to fund repairs through a shared toll, with the Wardens and the Hollow Circle watching the ledger.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_collapse"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Isles Owe","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Across the Sky","summary":"Grain moves openly to the isles under the reduced levy. Maris helps the Hollow Circle restock the granaries, and realises that hiding, like standing still, can be a brave act, even if it is no longer needed.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the Hollow's food supply under the new arrangement.","conflict":"Hunger has left scars, and Maris, who rarely forgives, must decide whether to trust Veya and Kael's bargain.","outcome":"Maris keeps her corridors secret but opens the granaries, and her friendship with Veya survives with honest terms.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_ledger","title":"Truths Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya publishes the full charts, including the error she once hid, and the Academy starts teaching them. She accepts recognition shared with Maris and the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Publish the charts and settle her mentor's legacy.","conflict":"Her pride and fear of becoming like the Cartel leaders pull against publishing an admission of wrong.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and her mentor's theory is accepted with her correction attached.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_docks_reckoning","title":"The Tollmaster's Bargain","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the isles gather to judge Kael. The Cartel is angry at his concession, the Hollow wants the toll abolished, and the Wardens say the bridges need his tolls. Kael accepts both blame and praise, his charm gone quiet.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle whether Kael remains toll-master under the shared arrangement.","conflict":"No one can agree whether he is villain or saviour. The tolls fund the bridges that also drain the Hollow.","outcome":"Kael keeps the post under shared oversight. The isles accept the bittersweet bargain, and Kael learns that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest","scn_silverspine_ledger"]}]}]}
