roost_crew","title":"The Shielded Pits","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya shows her chart to the Bridge Wardens and persuades them to send a repair crew with pre-braided cloudstone cable. The Wardens remind everyone that open flame is forbidden outside the shielded forge-pits, so the crew must work cold and by touch.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Assemble a repair crew and cable and get them to the weak span.","conflict":"The Wardens suspect Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies, so cable is scarce. Veya insists on leading the crew despite having no repair experience.","outcome":"The crew leaves with a limited stock of cable and a strict no-flame order. Veya has overpromised the repair.","depends_on":["scn_docks_offer"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_maris","title":"Grain and Secret Paths","summary":"The crew needs a shortcut around Cartel-watched lanes. Veya goes to The Hollow, where Maris is hiding grain from the Cartel levy. They trade wind-current knowledge for her unmapped service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a hidden route to the weak span. Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly. Cartel enforcers are already closing in on her smuggling routes, and helping Veya could expose them.","outcome":"Maris agrees to guide the crew through the service corridors and to ship her grain along the same path. Their alliance is sealed.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_crew"]},{"id":"scn_kael_pressure","title":"The Toll Closes","summary":"Kael closes the main lanes with a sudden toll and has his enforcers search for the crew. At the docks he sees that Veya's chart is accurate and realises the last stable routes will fall to whoever holds it.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize the last stable skybridge routes.","conflict":"He admires Veya's skill but cannot let her succeed. His belief that price equals worth makes him underestimate the Wardens and The Hollow.","outcome":"Kael sends enforcers after the crew's corridor route and takes personal charge of the chase.","depends_on":["scn_docks_offer","scn_hollow_maris"]},{"id":"scn_cold_span","title":"Working by Touch","summary":"On the failing skybridge, the crew braids new cable in the first snow. Without flame for warmth or light, hands go numb and a worker slips. Veya's wind-sight lets her predict the span's sway and pull the worker to safety.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Reinforce the weak span before the storm hits.","conflict":"The cold and darkness slow the work. When the crew's own chart is questioned, Veya cannot admit that her first estimate of the span's strength was wrong.","outcome":"The span is half-reinforced and the crew loses a full day. Veya is forced to accept Maris's correction, which damages her pride and her credibility with the crew.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_maris"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Storm Breaks","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_storm_confrontation","title":"No Fire Aloft","summary":"As the storm hits, Kael and his enforcers reach the span and demand the charts. Someone lights a torch against the dark, which risks severing the bridge. Veya and Kael must decide whether to fight over the charts or work together.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to finish the repair and keep the span standing. Kael wants her charts and control of the route.","conflict":"The enforcers' flame threatens to cut the span. Veya's pride and Kael's need for control keep each from yielding, and Maris's loyalty to The Hollow pulls her away from Veya.","outcome":"Veya hands Kael the chart. He orders the torch doused and joins the repair, and together they finish bracing the span as the storm passes. The Cartel's control over the route is broken.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pressure","scn_cold_span"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Wind","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wardens_accord","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Emberroost the Wardens copy Veya's charts for every isle. Kael faces the Cartel council and the Wardens over the sabotage accusation, and the Toll War begins to cool.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the charts so no one can hoard them. Kael wants to salvage his standing with the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael's colleagues call the charts a betrayal of the monopoly, and the Wardens demand that he answer for the sabotage.","outcome":"The charts are published openly. Kael concedes that control cost him more than it gained, and he accepts a Warden-supervised toll arrangement.","depends_on":["scn_storm_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_homecoming","title":"The Quiet Granary","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow. The levy is eased as part of the accord, and the grain she hid now feeds the isle openly. Veya visits to repay the wind-debt owed for the crossing.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to secure The Hollow's food and settle her friendship with Veya. Veya wants to repay her wind-debt.","conflict":"Maris is slow to forgive Veya's earlier pride, and Veya must admit she was wrong about the span.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake and Maris forgives her. Veya repays the debt with labour at the mills, and the isles stay joined through the winter.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_accord"]}]}]}

