 corridors between windmills and granaries to hide it from the Cartel's levy collectors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are already watching the corridors, and Maris's slow trust makes her refuse the help of her own neighbours.","outcome":"Maris saves one shipment but learns that enforcers have found part of her route, and she needs a way to reach other isles unseen.","depends_on":["scn_kael_tightens_tolls"]},{"id":"scn_kael_approaches_veya","title":"A Charming Offer","summary":"Kael travels to Silverspine and offers Veya funding and recognition in return for exclusive rights to her new charts. He admires her skill, and she is tempted by the praise.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to obtain Veya's charts. Veya wants to learn what he knows about the failing bridges.","conflict":"Veya's hunger for recognition pulls her toward the offer, but she fears becoming like the Cartel leaders and cannot admit that she needs his resources.","outcome":"Veya refuses to hand over the charts. Kael leaves with a veiled threat and the knowledge that she has already found a failing span.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_fading_bridge","scn_kael_tightens_tolls"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Breaking Bridges","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_seeks_maris","title":"Trading Paths for Winds","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow, where she meets Maris. They trade wind-current knowledge for knowledge of the secret service corridors and agree to help each other.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants access to unmapped routes for her chart. Maris wants a way to move grain past Cartel enforcers.","conflict":"Maris distrusts outsiders and demands proof of good faith, and Veya's stubbornness nearly ends the talks.","outcome":"They form an alliance. Veya's wind-sight reveals which corridors are safest, and Maris shares the location of an unmapped route toward Emberroost.","depends_on":["scn_maris_hides_grain","scn_kael_approaches_veya"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_wardens","title":"Cables of Cloudstone","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya shows the Bridge Wardens her charts of the failing spans. The Wardens accuse Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies of cloudstone, which would explain why the cables are weakening.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Convince the Wardens to reinforce the weakest skybridges using her charts.","conflict":"The Wardens lack cloudstone because supplies were diverted, and Veya refuses to admit that one of her readings was wrong, which costs her credibility.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to reinforce only one route. Veya realises that a safe path requires evidence of the Cartel's interference.","depends_on":["scn_veya_seeks_maris"]},{"id":"scn_kael_seizes_route","title":"The Docks Close","summary":"Kael uses the Cartel's hold on shipping lanes at Mistral Docks to block the Wardens' cloudstone shipments and to seize control of a stable crossing. His admiration for Veya is overtaken by his need to stop her.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable routes. Maris wants to slip a grain shipment through the docks.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery spots the weakness in Maris's smuggling arrangement, and she is caught in the open.","outcome":"Maris escapes but loses her cover and her grain, and Kael learns that Veya is working with her.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_wardens"]},{"id":"scn_veya_discovers_proof","title":"The Ledger Page","summary":"Using Maris's corridors and her own wind-sight, Veya reaches the Silverspine archive and finds Cartel shipping records that show Kael has been diverting cloudstone. She also finds that her chart contains an error she has refused to see.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find proof of the Cartel's sabotage and correct her charts.","conflict":"Admitting her error would shake her authority, and Maris warns that the corridors are being watched.","outcome":"Veya reluctantly corrects the chart and secures the proof, though she is tempted to hoard it. Maris insists she share it.","depends_on":["scn_kael_seizes_route"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_collapse","title":"The Hollow Falls Silent","summary":"The Cartel's blockade and the failing cables cause the bridge to The Hollow to sever. The isle is cut off just as the grain levy deadline arrives, and Maris must choose between her isle and her friendship with Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to get her people to safety. Kael wants to claim the levy. Veya wants to bring a route to the stranded.","conflict":"Maris, who trusts slowly, suspects Veya's charts caused the delay, and Kael uses the crisis to demand control of the surviving route.","outcome":"Veya shares her corrected chart openly, and Maris chooses to trust her. Kael realises that the proof she holds could end the Cartel's monopoly.","depends_on":["scn_veya_discovers_proof"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_climax_confrontation","title":"Confrontation on the Span","summary":"On the last stable skybridge near Emberroost, Veya and Kael meet. Veya has the proof and a safe route, and Kael has the Cartel's enforcers and a claim to the span.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to lead the stranded across and expose the sabotage. Kael wants to seize the route and bury her charts.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers press in, and the bridge begins to fail under the strain. Veya must choose between hoarding her charts to win and sharing them to save everyone.","outcome":"Veya broadcasts her chart and the proof to every crossing traveller, and Maris guides the crowd along her corridors. Kael sees that control would cost more than it gains and lets the span go.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_collapse"]},{"id":"scn_climax_crossing","title":"The Safe Route","summary":"As cables snap, Veya reads the wind and calls out the route, and Maris leads people through it. Kael decides to use his ledger-mastery to save the crossing rather than his monopoly.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get everyone across the failing skybridge before it falls.","conflict":"The forge-pits' sparks threaten to sever the final cable, and the old rivals must trust each other.","outcome":"Everyone crosses. The span falls behind them, and the Cartel's hold on the stable routes is broken in public view.","depends_on":["scn_climax_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_resolution_wardens","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes the corrected charts for the Wardens and the isles. She admits her earlier mistake publicly, and the Wardens begin to rebuild.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Share the charts so that every isle can use them.","conflict":"Some scholars want the charts restricted, and Veya must resist the urge to claim sole credit.","outcome":"The charts are placed in open archives, and the Wardens receive cloudstone to repair the bridges.","depends_on":["scn_climax_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_resolution_kael","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's princes after his monopoly is broken. He accepts reduced tolls and an inquiry into the diverted cloudstone.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the toll war on terms he can survive. Veya wants fair tolls for all crossings.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes blame Kael, and he must give up the power he spent years building.","outcome":"Kael agrees to lower tolls and share stable routes, and he and Veya part with grudging respect.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_wardens"]},{"id":"scn_resolution_hollow","title":"Quiet Windmills","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris watches the windmills turn again as the grain levy is lifted. She accepts Veya's friendship and understands that hiding was its own kind of courage.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore The Hollow's food supply and settle her loyalties.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive the Cartel and to trust the new arrangement.","outcome":"The Hollow is fed, the levy is lifted, and Maris and Veya remain allies as the isles continue to drift.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_kael"]}]}]}
