utcome":"Veya broadcasts her chart and the proof to every crossing traveller, and Maris guides the crowd along her corridors. Kael sees that control would cost more than it gains and lets the span go.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_collapse"]},{"id":"scn_climax_crossing","title":"The Safe Route","summary":"As cables snap, Veya reads the wind and calls out the route, and Maris leads people through it. Kael decides to use his ledger-mastery to save the crossing rather than his monopoly.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get everyone across the failing skybridge before it falls.","conflict":"The forge-pits' sparks threaten to sever the final cable, and the old rivals must trust each other.","outcome":"Everyone crosses. The span falls behind them, and the Cartel's hold on the stable routes is broken in public view.","depends_on":["scn_climax_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_resolution_wardens","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes the corrected charts for the Wardens and the isles. She admits her earlier mistake publicly, and the Wardens begin to rebuild.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Share the charts so that every isle can use them.","conflict":"Some scholars want the charts restricted, and Veya must resist the urge to claim sole credit.","outcome":"The charts are placed in open archives, and the Wardens receive cloudstone to repair the bridges.","depends_on":["scn_climax_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_resolution_kael","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's princes after his monopoly is broken. He accepts reduced tolls and an inquiry into the diverted cloudstone.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the toll war on terms he can survive. Veya wants fair tolls for all crossings.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes blame Kael, and he must give up the power he spent years building.","outcome":"Kael agrees to lower tolls and share stable routes, and he and Veya part with grudging respect.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_wardens"]},{"id":"scn_resolution_hollow","title":"Quiet Windmills","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris watches the windmills turn again as the grain levy is lifted. She accepts Veya's friendship and understands that hiding was its own kind of courage.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore The Hollow's food supply and settle her loyalties.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive the Cartel and to trust the new arrangement.","outcome":"The Hollow is fed, the levy is lifted, and Maris and Veya remain allies as the isles continue to drift.","depends_on":["scn_resolution_kael"]}]}]}
